sec.p:
The PUMCH ICU database was well-curated with very few (less than 3%) missing data of our analysis datasets. For the occasional missing values of patient temperature and replacement fluid, a mean substitution method was used for imputation of the missing data. After the missing data were filled in, the mean value of the variable remained unchanged. The data were normalized using min–max normalization method as follows:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
